   317	  // lookup above yields the event loop, so the id read before it is stale when this resumes; the db
   318	  // statement resolves the token inside itself and its `sqlColumn("claimed.id")` names the row it
   319	  // actually claimed. Reading the map again is the memory twin of that.
   320	  return (await claimAgentForHumanUserAfterLookup(claimToken, humanUserId, owner, events, priorLinks.find((link) => link.agent.id === claimTokenToAgentId.get(claimToken))?.linkRole, Boolean(human))).agent ?? null;
