   662	/**
   663	 * The before/after diff the db twin makes in SQL — the `moved` CTE, field for field.
   664	 *
   665	 * `display_name` is trimmed and an empty result clears the column, mirroring
   666	 * `NULLIF(BTRIM($5), '')`; `metadata` is MERGED and compared canonically, mirroring
   667	 * `p.metadata IS DISTINCT FROM (COALESCE(p.metadata,'{}') || $7)`. Sorted, because the db side
   668	 * aggregates `ORDER BY field`.
